WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.965
Detection is the point where the organization notices something that might be an incident.

00:00:04.965 --> 00:00:09.482
That signal might come from a security alert, an endpoint tool, cloud monitoring,

00:00:09.482 --> 00:00:14.347
identity logs, a user report, a vendor notification, threat intelligence, a data loss signal,

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.431
or an unusual business process event.

00:00:16.431 --> 00:00:18.864
Detection is not the same as confirmation.

00:00:18.864 --> 00:00:21.644
It is a prompt to ask better questions.

00:00:21.644 --> 00:00:22.339
What happened?

00:00:22.339 --> 00:00:25.466
Which system, user, service, or data set is involved?

00:00:25.466 --> 00:00:28.246
Is the activity expected, suspicious, or clearly harmful?

00:00:28.246 --> 00:00:32.068
Good detection provides context so analysts can prioritize the next step.

00:00:32.068 --> 00:00:36.585
A useful alert should point toward relevant evidence instead of just raising alarm.

00:00:36.585 --> 00:00:41.102
Weak detection creates delays and uncertainty: responders may learn about an incident late,

00:00:41.102 --> 00:00:45.620
lack the logs needed to scope it, or spend time chasing noisy signals.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.442
Detection engineering should therefore focus on meaningful coverage, clear alert descriptions,

00:00:49.442 --> 00:00:52.569
useful enrichment, and routing to people who can act.

00:00:52.569 --> 00:00:55.349
The goal is not to alert on everything.

00:00:55.349 --> 00:00:59.519
The goal is to notice important signals early enough that analysis and

00:00:59.519 --> 00:01:01.951
containment still have time to reduce impact.

00:01:01.951 --> 00:01:03.689
Detection also benefits from feedback.

00:01:03.689 --> 00:01:08.206
If analysts repeatedly close an alert as noise, the detection may need tuning.

00:01:08.206 --> 00:01:12.723
If responders keep asking for context that is not present, enrichment should improve.

00:01:12.723 --> 00:01:16.545
The best detection program learns from incidents, near misses, user reports,

00:01:16.545 --> 00:01:20.020
and false positives rather than treating alerts as fixed forever.
